# 0002. zinit as the only plugin manager, non-prompt plugins load turbo

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

One plugin manager, zinit, and everything not needed to draw the prompt loads right after
it appears.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: oh-my-zsh plus plugins loaded everything before the first prompt; startup was
  ~15x slower than now, while only oh-my-zsh's git library and git plugin aliases were used.
- **Bootstrap** (`conf.d/20-plugins.zsh`): `ZINIT[HOME_DIR]=$XDG_DATA_HOME/zinit`,
  `ZINIT[ZCOMPDUMP_PATH]=$ZSH_CACHE_DIR/zcompdump`; if `zinit.zsh` is missing it is cloned
  (`--depth=1`) from `zdharma-continuum/zinit`, the only network access, on first run only.
- **Loaded now**: `romkatv/powerlevel10k` (`depth=1`) then `p10k.zsh`;
  `zsh-users/zsh-completions` with `blockf` (adds to fpath before compinit). `Aloxaf/fzf-tab`
  loads in `30-completion.zsh` after compinit.
- **Loaded turbo** (`zinit wait lucid light-mode`):
  - `zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions` (`atload'_zsh_autosuggest_start'`, strategy
    `history completion`, buffer max 40, colour `#4a4c54`);
  - `zsh-users/zsh-history-substring-search`, bound to Up/Down and `^P`/`^N` in `atload`;
  - `zdharma-continuum/fast-syntax-highlighting`;
  - `OMZL::git.zsh` + `OMZP::git` snippets (oh-my-zsh's git library and aliases `gst`,
    `gco`, ...), then `lib/git.zsh` via `atload`.
- **Maintenance**: `make update` runs `zinit self-update && zinit update --all --parallel`,
  then `make clean` to rebuild caches.
- **Consequences**: the prompt appears before most plugins load. `zsh -ic` never reaches
  turbo plugins, so tests run `@zinit-scheduler burst` first (CLAUDE.md gotcha 1).
  oh-my-zsh's hundreds of git aliases can clash with helper names: an alias breaks
  `name() {` at parse time, so helpers use `function name {` plus `unalias name 2>/dev/null`.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: zinit (zdharma-continuum), powerlevel10k, zsh-completions, zsh-autosuggestions,
  zsh-history-substring-search, fast-syntax-highlighting, fzf-tab, oh-my-zsh snippets.
- Alternatives: full oh-my-zsh: slow, loads far more than used; antidote / sheldon / plain
  `source`: no deferred loading with the same control.
